Description:

The smmapd service now rejects a request whose netstring length is negative
or larger than the maximum request size, answering with a protocol error
instead of reading the request.  Previously the length was accepted up to the
limit of a 32-bit signed integer and then used as the number of bytes to read
into a fixed 1024-byte buffer on the stack, overflowing it.  smmapd is only
present where an administrator has configured it as a service, and it performs
no authentication of its own: it is intended to be reachable only from trusted
hosts, which is the boundary that protects it.

Tracked as GitHub security advisory GHSA-h85c-8j84-p3w5.


